    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0964" n="954" xml:id="pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3–146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-01T08:00:00+07:00">March 1, 1946—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 1—4:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>396. Situation changed by new exchange regulations promulgated February 25 and
                    going into effect on March 4. (ReEmbtel [<hi rendition="#italic">Deptel</hi>]
                    276 of February 13.) Provisions for functioning of appointed banks intended to
                    cover foreign banks. Adler will visit Shanghai next week and report<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d674-f1"/> on how regulations are working out with respect to
                    American banks and whether any further action necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d674-f1" n="85" xml:id="d674-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently no report was sent.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
